course: dictionary
lesson: 3460
title: Faint: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. Faint is a good example. «Children who skip breakfast find it harder to concentrate and can feel faint by mid-morning.» Here faint means weak and dizzy, as if you might fall.
explain: «Sound spreads out in every direction and gets weaker with distance, so a faraway shout is faint.» This faint means not strong or clear: it is hard to hear. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then pick the meaning that fits.
explain: Faint can also be a verb. «He got dizzy, his head pounded and he fainted.» Fainted means he suddenly became unconscious for a short time and fell down. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: Faint can mean very small too. «In 1610 Galileo turned a small telescope on the Milky Way and found it was made of countless faint stars.» Faint stars are hard to see. And «I haven't the faintest idea» means I don't know at all.
fact: Faint can be an adjective, a verb or a noun: faint, fainted, fainting, a faint.
fact: «Faint» means not strong or clear, hard to see, hear or smell.
fact: To faint means to suddenly become unconscious for a short time and fall down, often because the brain does not get enough blood.
fact: Feeling faint means feeling weak and dizzy; if you feel faint, sit down and tell an adult straight away.
fact: «Faint» can also mean very small, as in «a faint chance».
exercise: «Sound spreads out in every direction and gets weaker with distance, so a faraway shout is faint.» What does faint mean here? | *Not strong or clear, hard to hear | Heavy and slow | Very loud and clear | Full of happy shouts
exercise: «Children who skip breakfast can feel faint by mid-morning.» What does feel faint mean? | *Weak and dizzy, as if you might fall | Sleepy after a good night | Very cold and wet | Full of energy and ready to run
exercise: Which phrase uses faint to mean very small? | Loud and proud | *A faint chance | Long and thin | Bright and shiny
test: «A boy in Arizona ... he fainted.» What does fainted mean? | To shout loudly | To smell something sweet | To hurry home | *To suddenly become unconscious for a short time and fall down
test: Which word is a verb form of faint? | Faintest | *Fainted | Fainter | Faintly
exam: What does faint mean in «countless faint stars»? | Very loud | Very hot | *Not bright, hard to see | Dizzy and weak
